  (text "OpenMUPP v1 PIC high-voltage adapter (adapter ID slot 9, R1 = 91k 1 %)\nTargets: PIC ICSP, high-voltage and low-voltage entry. PICkit 4/5 8-pin: pins 1 to 6 are the same.\n\nJ1 plugs directly onto J4 of the OpenMUPP v1 probe. Pin numbers of J1 are the J4 pin numbers.\nJ4 pin 2 (reserved) stays open. J4 pin 16 (adapter ID) never goes to the target.\nReset circuit (MCLR_VPP): reset = AUX2 high (Q1 on, 0 V). Run = AUX2 low, VPP off (VTREF through R2).\nProgram = AUX2 low, VPP on (VPP from J4 pin 19). R3 holds Q1 off when AUX2 is high-impedance.\nFIRMWARE: never set AUX2 high while VPP is on. Q1 then shorts VPP to GND (current limit about 17 mA).\nBSS138 VGS(th) is up to 1.5 V: use VTREF of 1.8 V or more, or a lower-threshold FET.\nJ3 debug UART: labels are from the probe side (RX = probe input)."
    (at 30.48 40.64 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "8ebb0c90-90f4-4f08-bee6-63f3c16c79fe")
  )
